{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.removable_and_addable_exist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.removable_and_addable_exist","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/WeightedDirichletPoincare.lean#L204-L213","doc":"**The combinatorial core is not vacuous**: removable and addable corners both exist, just\nnever on one diagonal. The staircase-free partition `lam = (2, 1, 0, 0, …)` has a removable\ncorner at row `0` on diagonal `c = 1` and an addable corner at row `0` on diagonal `c = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.energy_lt_weighted_of_large_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.energy_lt_weighted_of_large_weight","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/WeightedDirichletPoincare.lean#L195-L202","doc":"**The inequality is not an equality.** The weight genuinely inflates the form when it\nexceeds 1 — so `weighted_ge_unweighted` is not secretly `rfl`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.weighted_lt_unweighted_of_small_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.weighted_lt_unweighted_of_small_weight","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/WeightedDirichletPoincare.lean#L186-L193","doc":"**`1 ≤ w` is load-bearing.** A single edge with weight `1/2` and increment `1` has\nweighted energy strictly below the unweighted energy, so the domination is false without the\nbound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.poincare_transfer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.poincare_transfer","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/WeightedDirichletPoincare.lean#L174-L182","doc":"**Poincaré transfer, at no loss of constant.**\n\nIf the *unweighted* form satisfies a Poincaré inequality `gap · V ≤ energy`, and every edge\nweight is at least 1, then the *weighted* form satisfies the same inequality with the **same**\n`gap`. This is the statement the `(|u|+|v|)`-weighted Fulman measure needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.weighted_ge_unweighted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.weighted_ge_unweighted","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/WeightedDirichletPoincare.lean#L165-L172","doc":"**A weight bounded below by 1 dominates.** No structure on the graph is used: only\n`1 ≤ w e` edgewise and `(d e)² ≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.energy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.energy","kind":"def","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/WeightedDirichletPoincare.lean#L162-L163","doc":"The unweighted Dirichlet energy `Σ_e (d e)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.weightedEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.weightedEnergy","kind":"def","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/WeightedDirichletPoincare.lean#L158-L160","doc":"The weighted Dirichlet energy `Σ_e w e · (d e)²`, with `d e` the increment across edge\n`e`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.one_le_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.one_le_weight","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/WeightedDirichletPoincare.lean#L134-L152","doc":"**The edge weight is at least 1.** Two distinct integer contents cannot both be zero, so\n`1 ≤ |u| + |v|`. Combined with `no_removable_addable_same_diagonal`, which is what rules out\n`u = v = 0` on an actual up-down edge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.no_removable_addable_same_diagonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.no_removable_addable_same_diagonal","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/WeightedDirichletPoincare.lean#L109-L132","doc":"**THE COMBINATORIAL CORE.** No partition has a removable corner and an addable corner on\nthe **same diagonal**.\n\nThis is what stops the edge weight `(|u| + |v|)` from vanishing: `|u| + |v| = 0` would put\nboth the removed and the added cell on the diagonal `c = 0`, which this forbids. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.Addable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.Addable","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/WeightedDirichletPoincare.lean#L103-L107","doc":"**Addable corner on diagonal `c`, at row `i`.**\n\nA new cell may be placed at `(i, lam i)`; its content is `c`, i.e. `lam i = i + c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.Removable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.Removable","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/WeightedDirichletPoincare.lean#L96-L101","doc":"**Removable corner on diagonal `c`, at row `i`.**\n\nThe cell `(i, lam i - 1)` is the last of its row and nothing sits below it in that column;\nits content is `c`, which in `ℤ` reads `lam i = i + c + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.antitone_of_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.antitone_of_step","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/WeightedDirichletPoincare.lean#L85-L94","doc":"`lam` is antitone as a function of the row index (the weakly-decreasing condition,\niterated). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.Antitone'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.WeightedDirichletPoincare.Antitone'","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/WeightedDirichletPoincare.lean#L82-L83","doc":"A partition is carried by its antitone row-length function `lam : ℕ → ℕ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}